Music at full quality while you listen.

Holding a headset's hands-free profile for a whole call drops everything you hear — the group and any music — to telephone bandwidth. MumbleWay now gives it back while you are only listening, and takes it again when you want to talk.

Turn on "Tap the phone to talk" in Settings to open the microphone by tapping the phone through a pocket or a bag. Off by default, so nothing changes until you ask for it.
